[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"comic_name":"intro_comic","purpose":"start"}"]
set {comic_complete} = false
label keeploading
[wait time="0.2"]
if {comic_complete} == false:
	if {page} == 0.0:
		if {panel} == 5.0:
			Narrator: [A woman's voice breaks through the static.]
			[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"purpose":"next_panel"}"]
			jump keeploading
	elif {page} == 1.0:
		if {panel} == 0.0:
			audio RadioClick "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
			Rose: -llo?
			[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"purpose":"next_panel"}"]
			jump keeploading
		elif {panel} == 2.0:
			Rose: Helloooo~?
			[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"purpose":"next_panel"}"]
			jump keeploading
	[wait_input]
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"purpose":"next_panel"}"]
	jump keeploading
audio WalkieBeep "res://assets/sfx/mp3/highpitchbeep.mp3" [volume="-10.0"]
Core/Jessie: H-hello? Is someone there?!
Rose: Hello? Oh my god, it worked? It actually worked?! Thank God!


audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
- Is this real?
	Core/Jessie: Is this really real?
	Rose: As real as it gets these days.
	Core/Jessie: But the radio tower...I thought it was broken.
	Rose: Me too, till I found a bit of duck tape and old electrical wire. Turns out rigging one of them things up ain't so hard after all.
	Core/Jessie: How does that even...n-nevermind. Does this mean you're in the city?
- Who is this?!
	Rose: I-what? I'm just—
	Core/Jessie: How do you know tis frequency? How do I know you're not—
	Rose: I'm not trying to trick you. I just—I fixed the radio tower. I've been broadcasting day and night, hoping someone would answer.
	Core/Jessie: ...
	Rose: I don't know where you are, and I can't get to you. I just wanted to know if anyone else was out there.
	Core/Jessie: You said you fixed the tower. So... you're in the city?
Rose: Well yeah, that’s where the repeater is located after all. This was..honestly my last hope for finding anyone. If this didn’t work I…anyway, I’m glad it worked.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Core/Jessie: Me too, frankly my situation is dire over here. I’m running low on everything. Plus, I’ve already looted everything I can from the nearby stores.
Core/Jessie: I’m not sure how much longer I can last out there. And I’m not thrilled about the idea of going into the city for a simple restock.
Rose: Yeah, it’s pretty bad. The streets are infested with infected, and all the chaos of the outbreak has left the city totally gridlocked with abandoned cars.
Rose: Not to mention the military’s poor attempt to control and quarantine. Leaving all their fences and barbed wire around.
Core/Jessie: ...
Rose: Sorry…didn’t mean to make things worse.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
- It's alright, I guess I'm just at a bit of a loss
	Core/Jessie: Don’t get me wrong, being able to talk to you - to anyone - is a big improvement. But it doesn’t change the situation.
	Rose: What situation? The one where it’s the end of the world and the Earth is infested with flesh eating zombies infected by some weird plant virus? That situation?
	Core/Jessie: Yes, that one.
	Core/Jessie: I just wish things were different…
	Rose: Doesn't everyone?
	Core/Jessie: I guess so, yeah. Sorry, I don’t mean to be such a debby downer.
	Rose: It’s hard not to be one in this kind of situation...
- Hey, at least you're honest.
	Core/Jessie: I appreciate not getting the "everything’s gonna be alright" speech.
	Rose: Yeah, that ship has sailed.
	Core/Jessie: Way past sailed. Pretty sure that ship crashed into the dock and got overrun.
	Rose: Oh my god.
	Core/Jessie: Too dark?
	Rose: Maybe. But I’ll allow it.
	Core/Jessie: Look, talking to someone[br]—even about barbed wire and gridlock—[br]is a hell of an improvement over talking to myself.
	Rose: Yeah. It really is.
Rose: So…I never asked your name.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Core/Jessie: Ah, right. My name’s Jessie.
Rose: Jessie huh? That’s a nice name. I bet you couldn’t guess what my name is.
Core/Jessie: Well, you’d be right about that.
Rose: Tch, talk about stingy. My name’s Rose. And yes, before you say anything, it’s like the lady from the Titanic.
Core/Jessie: Well, I’d make a joke about the tragedy but uh…feels a little too close to home right now.
Rose: I don’t really mind. Telling shitty jokes to the skeletons in my closet is the only thing that’s kept me going. I’d much rather tell shitty jokes with someone else.
Core/Jessie: Actual skeletons?
Rose: What? N-no, it’s a figure of speech…
Core/Jessie: R-right, I knew that.
Rose: You know…
Narrator: [Silence crackles on the other end for a moment]
audio WalkieBeep "res://assets/sfx/mp3/highpitchbeep.mp3"
Core/Jessie: Hello? Rose?
Rose: S-sorry, I was just thinking. It’s not important…
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Core/Jessie: Doesn’t sound like it.
Rose: Well…I know this is abrupt. And we met literally less than 5 minutes ago over a radio no less but…we could try to…meet up? 
Rose: I remember what I said about the streets, but I know them like the back of my hand.
Rose: I could guide you through the city no problem. And if you traveled while the sun is down I’m sure everything would be fine.
Rose: Ah…I’m getting ahead of myself, sorry.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
- No, no it's fine. Really, I...I would like that.
	Core/Jessie: Don’t get me wrong, the radio is a big improvement already. But…it would make the end of the world a whole lot less lonely if I had someone to share it with.
	Rose: Right?!
	Narrator: [Rose clears her throat in embarrasment]
	Rose: A-anyway, are you sure? I was sort of just…throwing it out there…
	Rose: I mean, don’t get me wrong, I’d do anything to talk face to face with a real person again. But you know…it’s dangerous, making that journey.
	Core/Jessie: Ma’am you’re talking to a certified firefighter. I’ve had my fair share of danger, what’s a little more?
- You want me to travel through a zombie-infested city to meet someone I've only known for five minutes?
	Rose: Well, when you say it like that, it sounds insane.
	Core/Jessie: That’s because it is insane.
	Rose: I know, I know. But—
	Core/Jessie: Rose, I don’t even know you. For all I know—
	Rose: I know. You’re right to be suspicious. I would be too.
	Core/Jessie: So why are you even suggesting this?
	Rose: Because I’m desperate. Because I’ve been alone for 9 months and talking to you is the first time I’ve felt human in weeks.
	Core/Jessie: ...
	Rose: And because…I think you need this too. Don’t you?
	Core/Jessie: ...Yeah. I do.
	Rose: So you’ll—?
	audio WalkieBeep "res://assets/sfx/mp3/highpitchbeep.mp3"
	Core/Jessie: I’ll do it. I’ll come to you.
	Rose: Really?
	Core/Jessie: Don’t make me change my mind. Look, I know it’s risky. I know I barely know you. But I can’t just stay here forever, and—
	Core/Jessie: —and I’m a firefighter. Or, I was. Running into danger is kind of what I do.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Rose: A firefighter, huh? Impressive…
Core/Jessie: Isn't it?
Rose: Alright, don’t go getting a big head about it now.
Narrator: [Rose takes a deep breath and loudly exhales before speaking again.]
Rose: Look, if you’re going to make it through this, you need to be prepared. And I don’t mean packing everything you could ever possibly carry. I mean the opposite.
Rose: Travel light. The faster you can move? The better.
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Rose: TThere’s no use fighting these things, hacking them apart doesn’t do anything but slow them down. So you’re better off avoiding them entirely.
Core/Jessie: How do you know so much about these things anyway?
Rose: Let’s just say it wasn’t a walk in the park repairing that repeater.
Core/Jessie: Alright, you’re the pro. I trust you.
Rose: Already? Didn’t your mom ever tell you not to trust strangers?
Core/Jessie: This isn’t some cliché action film. Sorry to say, but I generally have faith in people.
Rose: You shouldn't.
Core/Jessie: What?
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Rose: You’re going to be moving under the cover of night. That means it’ll take at least a few days to get here. You’ll have to camp out in some places—
Rose: —so be sure to bring something you can use to protect yourself with. But only as a precaution, nothing more. Remember, fighting is a last resort.
Core/Jessie: I’ve got an old flashlight I’ve been using on my supply runs, and a rusty hatchet I used for chopping up the wood to board my doors and windows with.
Core/Jessie: But…that flashlight might need some new batteries.
Rose: Shit...
Core/Jessie: Don’t worry, I think I know just the place…
Rose: Thank god. Alright, I’ll let you get ready. We can talk about the next steps once you’re done.
Core/Jessie: Rodger that.
Rose: ...
audio "res://assets/sfx/adjustedvolume/-20 dB/radio_click.wav"
Jessie: (Aside) Why did I say that…
set {opening_finished} = true
[signal arg="nextpage"]